<spell-notebook "content-parts theming">
	<header level="1">
		Content parts
		<header>Headers, content, descriptions, metas and the other generic parts that cards, items, modals and
              messages share.</>
	</>
	<content-parts-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			A standalone header's tokens are public (`--ui-header-*`): set one on the element, on any ancestor or `:root`, or
			through `::part(header)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a private alias.

			- The page header ladder (`--ui-header-h1` ... `-h6`) is a ratio of `--ui-font-size`; the content header ladder
			  (`--ui-header-size-mini` ... `-massive`) is in `em` of the surrounding text.
			- Inside an owner, a part's look comes from the OWNER's tokens (`--ui-card-header-color`,
			  `--ui-modal-header-size` ...): set them on the owner or above it, and every part inside follows. See each
			  owner's Theming tab.
			- Never set the private switches owners hand their parts (`--_ui-card-layout` ...), or any `--_*` name.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* quieter page headers everywhere */
			:root {
			  --ui-header-font-weight: 600;
			  --ui-header-h1: 1.75;
			}
			/* one card's header */
			ui-card.note {
			  --ui-card-header-color: var(--ui-primary);
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-parts" playground>
				<ui-header level="1">First header</>
				<ui-header level="2">Second header</>
				<ui-header level="3">Third header</>
				<ui-header level="4">Fourth header</>
				<ui-header level="5">Fifth header</>
				<ui-header level="6">Sixth header</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling these parts through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
